================================================================================================================
L154 -- where the pincer actually is: Lyman-alpha vs galaxies, and the verdict on the GDM loophole
================================================================================================================

================================================================================================================
PART 0 -- THE SOLVER, AND ITS VALIDATION AGAINST CLASS.
================================================================================================================
  Sub-horizon linear system for the dark fluid (delta_d) and the baryons (delta_b), in ln a:
      delta'' + (2 + dlnE/dlna) delta' = (3/2) a^-3 [Om_d delta_d + Om_b delta_b]/E^2  -  J delta
  with the fluid's Jeans term J = c_s^2(a) k^2/(a H)^2 acting on delta_d only.  c_s^2(a) is ARBITRARY.
  Initial conditions: growing mode at a_i = 1e-3.  Reported quantity = the BARYON power ratio, which is
  what the Lyman-alpha forest actually traces, and what CLASS's mPk returns in this configuration.

         c_s^2     k |  CLASS z=0    solver |  CLASS z=3    solver
         1e-08   0.5 |     0.9818    0.9822 |     0.9942    0.9945
         1e-08   1.0 |     0.9295    0.9309 |     0.9770    0.9783
         1e-08   2.0 |     0.7513    0.7561 |     0.9118    0.9165
         1e-08   5.0 |     0.2258    0.2354 |     0.5766    0.5963
         1e-07   0.5 |     0.8346    0.8379 |     0.9437    0.9468
         1e-07   1.0 |     0.5061    0.5144 |     0.7962    0.8067
         1e-07   2.0 |     0.1266    0.1350 |     0.4279    0.4517
         1e-07   5.0 |     0.0094    0.0132 |     0.0458    0.0633
         1e-06   0.5 |     0.2260    0.2354 |     0.5767    0.5963
         1e-06   1.0 |     0.0366    0.0426 |     0.1650    0.1893
         1e-06   2.0 |     0.0045    0.0074 |     0.0222    0.0362
         1e-06   5.0 |     0.0001    0.0011 |     0.0005    0.0055

      disagreement in the DECISIVE band (CLASS ratio > 0.3, where the 0.90 gate acts): max 5.57 percent
      sign of the residual: the solver retains at least as much power as CLASS in 24/24 cases
      -- i.e. the solver is uniformly OPTIMISTIC (it under-states the suppression), which is the
      generous direction for the loophole, so the kill below is not an artifact of the solver.
  [PASS] VAL-1  the arbitrary-c_s^2(a) two-fluid solver reproduces CLASS's exact Boltzmann integration of the constant-c_s^2 GDM system to better than 6 percent throughout the band where the gates below actually act (power ratio above 0.3), and it NEVER under-states the retained power -- it is uniformly generous to the loophole.  It is therefore fit to evaluate profiles CLASS cannot run (time-dependent c_s^2), and cannot manufacture the kill   (max disagreement 5.57 percent for ratio > 0.3; solver >= CLASS in all 24 comparisons (generous direction))

================================================================================================================
PART 1 -- THE INTERMEDIATE-EPOCH GATE: the Lyman-alpha forest at z = 2-5, k up to ~8 Mpc^-1.
================================================================================================================
  Neither of L125's gates touches 3 < z < 1000.  But the Lyman-alpha forest measures the 1D flux power
  spectrum at z = 2-5 out to k ~ 0.1 s/km, which at z = 3 is k ~ 7.7 Mpc^-1 comoving.  A dark fluid with
  a sound speed erases power on exactly those scales, and the erasure is worst at LATE times because
  a H falls -- so a profile designed to be hot today is warm at z = 3.

      calibration of the Lyman-alpha tolerance.  The published 95 percent thermal-WDM limit
      m_WDM > 5.3 keV corresponds, through the Bode-Ostriker-Turok transfer function, to a 3D
      power suppression of P/P_CDM = 0.961 at k = 8 Mpc^-1 = 11.9 h/Mpc (and 0.9991 at k = 1.5 Mpc^-1).
      So the data actually tolerate about 4 percent at the outer wavenumber.  The
      fiducial gate below uses 0.90 -- LOOSER than the data by a factor 2.6 -- and the calibrated
      value is carried as a sensitivity row.  No deficit is manufactured by the choice.

          p   cs(1)=207   cs(1)=300   cs(1)=500   cs(1)=900     (baryon P(k=8)/P_CDM at z=3)
        0.0      0.0047      0.0029      0.0020      0.0016
        1.0      0.2445      0.1538      0.0793      0.0365
        2.0      0.8025      0.6697      0.4752      0.3044
        3.0      0.9749      0.9491      0.8745      0.7145
        4.0      0.9968      0.9934      0.9821      0.9457
        5.0      0.9996      0.9991      0.9975      0.9920
  [PASS] LYA-1  the intermediate epochs are where the constraint lives.  A CONSTANT-sound-speed fluid at the galaxy-gate minimum (c_s = 207 km/s, which passes BOTH of L125's gates with room to spare) erases essentially all z = 3 power at k = 8 Mpc^-1.  Only a steeply GROWING c_s^2 restores it -- so the loophole is forced back into needing growth after all, but now over a lever arm of 4 in a, not 1090   (p=0: P/P_CDM = 0.0047 (excluded);  p=4 at the same c_s(1): 0.9968 (allowed))

