  GATE-G  the L61 galaxy gate, with L153's THEOREM B.  A barotropic fluid with c_s^2 ~ a^p is the
          polytrope P = A rho^Gamma, Gamma = 1 - p/3.  In a MOND logarithmic potential it has a
          condensation front at r_crit = r_ref exp(-3 c_s^2(1)/(p v_c^2)) inside which there is NO
          hydrostatic solution.  GENEROUS implementation: the front is ALLOWED to sit inside r_in =
          10 kpc (whatever mass condenses there is simply not counted), and the enclosed fluid mass is
          integrated only over 10-100 kpc and compared with the L61 0.11 dex tolerance.
